  m_Name: BallValveData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: 'Ball Valve '
  engineDescription: 'A Ball Valve is a quarter-turn mechanical valve used to control,
    isolate, or regulate the flow of liquids and gases in piping systems. It operates
    using a spherical ball with a central bore that rotates 90 degrees to either
    allow or block the flow. Its main components include the valve body, ball, stem,
    seats, seals, actuator or handle, bonnet, and end connections. During operation,
    rotating the handle or actuator turns the ball so that the bore aligns with the
    pipeline for full flow or rotates perpendicular to stop the flow completely.
    The seats provide a tight seal, ensuring reliable shut-off with minimal leakage.


    Ball
    valves are widely used in oil and gas, chemical processing, water treatment,
    power generation, HVAC, and industrial piping systems due to their durability,
    low pressure drop, and quick operation.'
  engineCategory: Engineering
